# Rows to merge into docs/TECH-DEBT.md

Source: Phase 1 for `play/src/pusher/services/SocketManager.ts` (2026-11-12). Baseline `HEAD` = `1f48d79d5`, `SocketManager.ts` sha256 `de35ca77…09c68673`. Evidence: `docs/audits/tech-debt/phase1-socketmanager/README.md`. Line numbers are `HEAD`'s.

## Debt Ledger rows

| Item | Location | Type | Risk | Effort | Priority | Status |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| SM-01: `handleUserMovesMessage` writes the move to the back before it checks the viewport. A move without a viewport reaches the back, then the handler throws `Missing viewport in UserMovesMessage`, and the zones stay where they were. | `SocketManager.ts:668-689` | quirk (validation after the side effect) | low. `RoomConnection.sharePosition` always sends a viewport, so only a hand-made client hits it. Each such move costs one Sentry report through the controller's catch. | XS (check first, or parse at the boundary) | P3 | pinned ("SM-01 (pinned): forwards a move without a viewport…"); no fix planned before Phase 2 |
| SM-02: a `roomJoinedMessage` that the back sends after the pusher closed the socket still subscribes the socket's viewport. The `data` handler checks `isDisconnecting()` only before the relay. The `end` handler that follows does nothing for a disconnecting socket, so the zones are never released, `isEmpty()` stays false, and the room and its `listenRoom` stream stay open after the last real socket leaves. The closed socket also stays a zone listener and receives every event of its zones. | `SocketManager.ts:283-301` (handler), `:650-666` (`handleViewport`), `PusherRoom.ts:37-42` (`setViewport`) | bug (resource leak) | medium. Needs a close started by the pusher (`closeWebsocketConnection` on a failed join or a back error) while the join is unanswered. Reachability is inferred from the code; no production log shows it. Each leak keeps one room stream and its zone subscriptions until the pusher restarts. | XS (one guard) | P1 | zones and room fixed by `fix-SM-02.patch` (`PusherRoom.setViewport` ignores a socket that is not in the room); pinned in `characterization-tests.patch`, test flipped. Still open: the late message also calls `analyticsTimedEventTracker.open` after `closeConnection` ran, so that session is never closed (inferred; the tests stub `open`) |
| SM-03: on a client-initiated close (codes 1000 and 1001), `cleanupSocket` runs twice. The controller's `close` handler calls it without setting `isDisconnecting()`, and the back stream's later `end` runs `closeWebsocketConnection`, which calls it again. Each socket ends its gRPC stream twice and runs `leaveSpaces` twice. | `SocketManager.ts:615-648`, `:318-346`; `PusherRoomSocketController.ts:364-395`; `IoSocketController.ts:1161` | design (idempotence by accident) | low today: `joinedRoom` and the forwarder's in-flight map keep the leave events and space removals single (`SocketManagerClientGauge.test.ts`). Every later change to cleanup must stay idempotent. | S | P2 | not pinned (inferred from the code) |
| SM-04: each browser socket opens its own bidirectional gRPC stream to the back (`apiClient.connectToRoom()`), and every move and message for that user goes through it. 1,000 users on one pusher means 1,000 streams to the backs, besides one `listenRoom` stream per room. | `SocketManager.ts:270-271` | performance / scaling (1,000 users) | medium. The cost is per connection in memory and in HTTP/2 stream limits per channel. Not measured. | L (multiplex per room, a protocol change) | P3 | open; test 1 pins one stream per socket and one per room |
| SM-05: a zone event is fanned out with one `emitInBatch` per watching socket (`Zone.notify*` into `SocketManager.onUserMoves` and the other callbacks). In a room where N users all see each other, one move costs N-1 calls, and a tick where everyone moves costs about N² calls. Each socket encodes its own batch when it flushes, so the same move is encoded N-1 times. | `Zone.ts:296-395`, `SocketManager.ts:691-728`, `:1046-1097` | performance / scaling (1,000 users) | medium to high for dense rooms. This is the pusher's share of the 1,000-user cost. Not measured. | M (encode once per zone and share the bytes, or cap the watchers) | P2 | open; the fan-out test pins one message per watcher and none for the user itself |
| SM-06: the `SocketManager` constructor adds four listeners to the global `clientEventsEmitter` and never removes them. Each `new SocketManager()` in a test adds four more, so the gauges count once per instance. | `SocketManager.ts:110-123` | test debt / hidden global | low. Production builds one instance. The test files call `new SocketManager(` 18 times (9 in the new file, 9 in six older files), and vitest isolates each file. | S (inject the emitter, or register in the module) | P3 | open |
| SM-07: `PusherRoom` imports the `socketManager` module singleton to clean up its sockets when its back stream fails, and `SocketManager` imports `PusherRoom`. A test cannot give a room its own manager, so the room's `error` and `close` paths always call the singleton. | `PusherRoom.ts:9`, `:234-265`; `SocketManager.ts:62`, `:1822` | design / coupling | low | S (pass the `ZoneEventListener`, which is already the manager, or a cleanup callback) | P3 | open; the gap that leaves the room's `error` and `close` paths without a test |

